three months ago now.

00:06:52.410 --> 00:06:54.760
So we're fairly
new to the program.

00:06:54.760 --> 00:06:58.440
And what it means is we're
recognized by Google.

00:06:58.440 --> 00:07:03.420
There is about I believe
250 of us worldwide.

00:07:03.420 --> 00:07:05.490
So we're recognized
for our expertise

00:07:05.490 --> 00:07:08.990
in a specific area of Google
technology as their products.

00:07:08.990 --> 00:07:11.490
In our case, it's
Google Cloud Platform.

00:07:11.490 --> 00:07:12.870
We do a lot of blogging.

00:07:12.870 --> 00:07:14.840
We go and talk at conferences.

00:07:14.840 --> 00:07:16.970
We help the local community.

00:07:16.970 --> 00:07:18.300
We help startups.

00:07:18.300 --> 00:07:19.930
We do mentoring.

00:07:19.930 --> 00:07:22.484
And we also get a yearly trip.

00:07:22.484 --> 00:07:24.900
Once a year, we get to meet
all the other Google Developer

00:07:24.900 --> 00:07:27.130
experts, which is really cool.

00:07:27.130 --> 00:07:29.770
This year it was
in Mountain View

00:07:29.770 --> 00:07:32.720
just last month,
which is really cool.

00:07:32.720 --> 00:07:33.470
MARK MANDEL: Yeah.

00:07:33.470 --> 00:07:34.740
I saw you guys there.

00:07:34.740 --> 00:07:35.573
GRAHAM POLLEY: Yeah.

00:07:35.573 --> 00:07:38.640
We get direct access to the
engineering teams as well.

00:07:38.640 --> 00:07:41.527
So we get early access to builds
and features and new products

00:07:41.527 --> 00:07:42.360
and stuff like that.

00:07:42.360 --> 00:07:44.810
And we can reach out directly
to the engineering teams.

00:07:44.810 --> 00:07:46.920
