00:08:09.320 --> 00:08:11.530
And we were just blown
away by how cool it was

00:08:11.530 --> 00:08:13.410
and how much data we
could smash through.

00:08:13.410 --> 00:08:15.140
And we wrote a blog about it.

00:08:15.140 --> 00:08:18.040
And that blog got picked
up by our good friend

00:08:18.040 --> 00:08:20.564
Philippe Hoffa, who I believe
you guys know quite well.

00:08:20.564 --> 00:08:21.480
FRANCESC CAMPOY: Yeah.

00:08:21.480 --> 00:08:24.020
We interviewed him
two episodes ago.

00:08:24.020 --> 00:08:24.440
MARK MANDEL: Yeah,
something like that.

00:08:24.440 --> 00:08:25.640
GRAHAM POLLEY: Ah,
two episodes ago.

00:08:25.640 --> 00:08:26.110
Yeah.

00:08:26.110 --> 00:08:26.610
Cool.

00:08:26.610 --> 00:08:27.350
So.

00:08:27.350 --> 00:08:29.070
Yeah, Philippe's a great guy.

00:08:29.070 --> 00:08:30.690
And he actually
picked up our blog.

00:08:30.690 --> 00:08:32.890
He found our blog.

00:08:32.890 --> 00:08:34.530
And he shared it internally.

00:08:34.530 --> 00:08:38.590
And then it actually went-- It
made its way up to Urs Holzle,

00:08:38.590 --> 00:08:40.763
who then re-shared
it on his G+ page.

00:08:40.763 --> 00:08:41.679
FRANCESC CAMPOY: Nice.

00:08:41.679 --> 00:08:43.095
GRAHAM POLLEY: And
then from there

00:08:43.095 --> 00:08:44.970
