00:27:04.440 --> 00:27:07.720
There's a lot of people that try
to do things like integration

00:27:07.720 --> 00:27:10.340
tests or even
continuous integration,

00:27:10.340 --> 00:27:13.310
when what you're trying to
do is to deploy continuously.

00:27:13.310 --> 00:27:14.060
MARK MANDEL: Yeah.

00:27:14.060 --> 00:27:16.767
FRANCESC CAMPOY: And deploying
continuously, it's pretty hard.

00:27:16.767 --> 00:27:17.850
There is ways of doing it.

00:27:17.850 --> 00:27:20.070
But you know, there's
a skill there.

00:27:20.070 --> 00:27:23.620
Then there's deploying
continuously to App Engine.

00:27:23.620 --> 00:27:25.990
And all of a sudden, it doesn't
sound that easy anymore,

00:27:25.990 --> 00:27:28.500
because you have to use G cloud.

00:27:28.500 --> 00:27:30.240
And there's a bunch
of things that you

00:27:30.240 --> 00:27:33.040
have to integrate,
authentication, and so on.

00:27:33.040 --> 00:27:35.560
So the question was,
like, is there an easy way

00:27:35.560 --> 00:27:37.614
to do deployment swap engine?

00:27:37.614 --> 00:27:39.280
MARK MANDEL: Like
say, programmatically?

00:27:39.280 --> 00:27:39.600
FRANCESC CAMPOY: Yeah.

00:27:39.600 --> 00:27:40.940
As part of the script,
something that's

00:27:40.940 --> 00:27:42.690
going to be happening
very regularly.

00:27:42.690 --> 00:27:45.810
MARK MANDEL: So I got shown
this not too long ago.

00:27:45.810 --> 00:27:47.310
And I found it quite exciting.

00:27:47.310 --> 00:27:50.020
There is an API
that we have that

00:27:50.020 --> 00:27:52.724
enables you to programmatically
deploy to App Engine.

00:27:52.724 --> 00:27:53.640
FRANCESC CAMPOY: Nice.

00:27:53.640 --> 00:27:55.290
MARK MANDEL: It's really cool.

00:27:55.290 --> 00:27:57.760
It's both a REST
API and a gRPC API.

00:27:57.760 --> 00:28:02.860
So you have a choice,
whichever one you want to use.

00:28:02.860 --> 00:28:03.760
It's pretty cool.

00:28:03.760 --> 00:28:05.520
You can upload your
content-- like so

00:28:05.520 --> 00:28:08.640
basically your resources up
into Google Cloud Storage.

00:28:08.640 --> 00:28:12.760
You send up a JSON manifest
file to tell App Engine hey,

00:28:12.760 --> 00:28:13.844
this is where my stuff is.

00:28:13.844 --> 00:28:15.176
This is how I want to deploy it.

00:28:15.176 --> 00:28:16.430
This is where I want it to go.

00:28:16.430 --> 00:28:18.370
And then it goes off
and does its thing.

00:28:18.370 --> 00:28:20.230
And then there's also stuff
in there for like switching

00:28:20.230 --> 00:28:20.729
modules.

00:28:20.729 --> 00:28:22.800
So which modules
you want to go to.

00:28:22.800 --> 00:28:25.550
And like also doing your
standard versioning stuff too.

00:28:25.550 --> 00:28:27.980
Like, I want 50% of my
traffic to go to this one.

00:28:27.980 --> 00:28:30.750
Or 10%, or 100%.

00:28:30.750 --> 00:28:31.250
Yeah.

00:28:31.250 --> 00:28:32.480
And also introspection.

00:28:32.480 --> 00:28:33.950
You can also do
introspection through it too.

00:28:33.950 --> 00:28:35.270
Like, what have I got running.

00:28:35.270 --> 00:28:36.380
What versions do I have?

00:28:36.380 --> 00:28:38.350
What apps do I have?

00:28:38.350 --> 00:28:39.160
It's pretty neat.

00:28:39.160 --> 00:28:40.900
I was actually really
impressed with it.

00:28:40.900 --> 00:28:42.500
So if you're looking at doing
like continuous delivery

00:28:42.500 --> 00:28:45.041
type of stuff, and you want to
be able to push to App Engine,

00:28:45.041 --> 00:28:47.010
this looks like a really
good way of doing it.

00:28:47.010 --> 00:28:47.210
FRANCESC CAMPOY: Yeah.

00:28:47.210 --> 00:28:48.210
That sounds really cool.

00:28:48.210 --> 00:28:50.690
I could definitely
see it as something

00:28:50.690 --> 00:28:54.000
integrated early with Jenkins or
Travis or something like that.

00:28:54.000 --> 00:28:56.150
So basically as long as
you have a new file that

00:28:56.150 --> 00:28:59.120
has changed, everything,
you get a bunch of tests.

00:28:59.120 --> 00:29:00.380
It gets deployed somewhere.

00:29:00.380 --> 00:29:02.957
And then someone can
just go and verify

00:29:02.957 --> 00:29:04.040
that everything's working.

